	\end{equation} 
	Summing~\eqref{consecutive gap} from $k=k_0$ to an arbitrary $l\geq k_0+1$ and passing $l$ to infinity justifies~\eqref{finite length}.
	A similar procedure shows that $\seq{x^k}$ is Cauchy, which together with \cref{thm:subseq:omega} entails the rest of the statement. 
\end{proof}

